==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|spedi|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|spēdiġ||having good speed, lucky, prosperous; having means, wealthy, opulent, rich in material wealth; rich in, abounding in, abundant, plenteous, copious; powerful}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*spōdigaz||successful, hurried}}, equivalent to {{suffix|speed|y|lang=en}}. Cognate with {{etyl|sco|-}} {{term|spedie||speedy|lang=sco}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|spoedig||speedy, swift, rapid, quick|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|sputig|lang=de}}, {{term|spudig||industrious, speedy|lang=de}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈspi:di/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|iːdi|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# Characterized by a [[rapid]] or [[swift]] motion.

====Synonyms====
* [[fast]], [[swift]], [[quick]], [[rapid]]
* See also [[Wikisaurus:speedy]]

====Derived terms====
* [[speedily]]
* [[speediness]]
* [[speedy delete]]
* [[speedy deletion]]

